//! **Option B, step three — A4 and A5 for the designated target.**
//!
//! `level::Level::is_zero` as the compiler emits it, with a labelled model of
//! the one callee no artifact can carry a body for, proved correct against the
//! reflected `level_is_zero` for every `Level` and every representing heap.
//!
//! Closes link 4, which `ir_lz_minted_refutes_a4_on_max` measured OPEN on
//! 2026-08-22. The residual is named in `ir_lzb_correct`'s registration and
//! is not discharged: the deref model is an assumption, and A0's bodyful
//! reachable closure stays blocked by rustc having no cross-crate THIR.
//!
//! ## The relation describes the machine's heap, not the model's
//!
//! `EncodesLevelArcF`'s three recursive arms place each child `Level` at
//! `Nat.add b ir_d16` — sixteen cells past the pointer STORED in the field,
//! where `<Arc<T> as Deref>::deref` looks — rather than at `b` itself. Audit
//! r16 M16-6 (2026-09-02) measured that the earlier reading, which put the
//! child at `b`, made the relation UNSATISFIABLE by any real `Level` heap at
//! exactly the `Succ`/`Max`/`IMax` nodes this module's content is about: the
//! model computed `x` where the machine computes `&*x`. The model now carries
//! the `gep` and the relation moved with it, so the two describe one heap.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

